      "description": "Watch Cambuur vs Excelsior highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The atmosphere was electric on August 8, 2026 , as Cambuur hosted Excelsior in a clash that promised tactical intrigue. Both sides took to the pitch desperate to secure early momentum in this Eredivisie encounter. Excelsior's Clinical First Half The visitors wasted no time asserting their dominance, breaking the deadlock in the 17th minute. Irakli Yegoian found the back of the net with a composed right-footed finish following a sharp assist from Gyan de Regt . Excelsior continued to pile on the pressure, and their persistence paid off in the 31st minute when Noah Naujoks doubled the lead with a clinical left-footed strike, set up by the goalscorer Yegoian . Just before the interval, Excelsior effectively put the game out of reach. In the 42nd minute, Simon Janssen played a short corner that eventually found its way to David Garden , who rose highest to power a header home. The home side, Cambuur , looked shell-shocked as they headed into the halftime break trailing by three goals after a masterclass in finishing from the visitors. Second Half Consolidation Cambuur attempted to shift the tide at the restart, introducing Morgan Costarelli and Sami Bouhoudane to inject some energy into the midfield. Despite their efforts to create openings, Excelsior remained disciplined and organized. The visitors extended their lead further in the 69th minute when Noah Naujoks connected with another Simon Janssen delivery, this time heading the ball into the net to secure his second goal of the match. Late VAR Intervention The closing stages were characterized by a flurry of tactical substitutions as Excelsior looked to see out the result. There was a brief concern for Iwan Henstra , who required medical attention in the 84th minute, but he was able to continue as the clock ticked down. In stoppage time, Excelsior thought they had added a fifth through Ilano Silva Timas , but the celebrations were cut short when the referee, following a review, ruled the goal out for offside. The match concluded shortly after, leaving the traveling fans delighted with a comprehensive performance on August 8, 2026 , while Cambuur will be left to rue a difficult day at the office."
